    schema:datePosted "2026-09-11"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About MUBI MUBI is a global streaming service, production company and film distributor dedicated to elevating great cinema. To make this possible, we create, curate, acquire and champion visionary films, bringing them to audiences all over the world. We have a team of brilliant, dedicated and passionate people to help bring our mission to life. From London to New York, Istanbul to Paris, and Berlin to Mexico - we work together to realize MUBI’s vision. That’s where you come in! Join our global team and help us make great cinema accessible to everyone, everywhere. About the Role As a MUBI SHOP Intern, you will work alongside the Senior Digital Commerce Manager and build close partnerships across Creative, Logistics, and Marketing (Social & CRM) to drive the global growth of MUBI SHOP through day-to-day operations. You’ll be hands-on with sales reports & forecasting, e-merchandising, inventory management, merch conception, fulfilment operations, UX design and customer communications via Marketing & Customer Support. Working across diverse e-commerce functions will equip you with practical, comprehensive insights into MUBI SHOP operations - developing deep proficiency in Shopify, operations and the product life-cycle within the film industry. We work hybrid-remote where we require 3 office days in London. Our core days are Tuesday, Wednesday & Thursday, with the flexibility to use our offices on the remaining two days if you wish. Where you’ll have impact: Shopify & E-Merchandising: Support with product uploads & deactivation, e-merchandising and UX improvements within Shopify. Operations & Logistics: Work closely with the Customer Support team, updating them on our new merch drops, providing operational updates, and handling routine admin. Administrative Support: Manage sales/invoice coordination and basic administrative tasks to keep SHOP operations running smoothly. Marketing & CRM: Assist with basic marketing tasks, such as proofreading copy, reviewing Creative assets, testing links for campaigns, and updating CRM/social media projects. Cross-functional Communication: Coordinate with internal/external Global teams to ensure product information is received on time, work closely with merch conception and production, support with brand partnerships, collaborate with local teams for specific market adaptations for SHOP. Website Maintenance: Perform routine website checks to ensure links are working, content is displayed correctly; report any issues to the team. What you’ll bring: Communication: Communicate clearly and respectfully with colleagues; ask questions when unsure rather than guessing. Growth Mindset: Eager to learn new tools and processes; receptive to feedback and keen to apply learnings to future tasks. Collaboration: Participate in team discussions and rituals; support the team by taking on small administrative tasks with a positive attitude. Ownership: Take ownership of assigned tasks from start to finish; review existing documentation and past examples before escalating questions. Functional Expertise: Develop foundational knowledge of e-commerce platforms and fulfilment workflows by assisting with QA and operational execution. Enthusiasm for MUBI and e-commerce. Proactive, positive, and helpful attitude. Strong attention to detail. Willingness to learn and contribute to a collaborative team environment. Duration: 3 months Stipend: £500 per month Location: London We want to make cinema accessible to everyone. We believe people from different backgrounds bring different ideas that foster innovation and engagement, allowing us to attract great people to develop the best experience for our users. MUBI is committed to being an Equal Opportunity Employer. That means it's our responsibility to ensure that all candidates are not discriminated against in our hiring processes and our employment decisions based on their race, color, religion, nationality or ethnic origin, age, gender identity or expression, sex, marital status, physical or mental disability, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, family or parental status, or any other applicable characteristic. Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
