    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-integrated-producer-berlin-108438" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-12"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "At Jellyfish, we believe in the power of diverse perspectives and inclusive collaboration. We welcome individuals who excel in collaborative, varied teams and value the unique contributions that each person brings to the table. Jellyfish is a global digital marketing agency; a unique fusion of tech enthusiasts, creative minds, and media and data experts all united to empower our clients along their digital journey. Our commitment to embracing diverse perspectives fuels our innovation and strategies that challenge the status quo, reinvent media activation, and craft influential stories for our global clients and their customers. Join us in shaping a future where business growth and personal fulfilment go hand in hand Job Description As a Senior Integrated Producer, you will be responsible for leading the end-to-end production process, ensuring seamless execution, financial oversight, and stakeholder coordination. You are expected to balance project management and production expertise, delivering high-budget, complex, and multi-market projects while driving efficiencies, mentorship, and strategic problem-solving. You will collaborate closely with Client Management, Resource Management, and Creative teams, acting as a trusted production lead while maintaining financial and operational control over projects. Working on a high-profile social media retainer for a titan in the global streaming and entertainment sector, you will sit at the absolute heart of our German market operations. This role is ideal for a producer who thrives in client-facing environments, enjoys hands-on workflow coordination, and brings a strong project management background to fast-paced agency retainers. Your primary responsibilities will include: Client & Stakeholder Management: Act as the primary, trusted client-facing lead for German market operations - building strong direct relationships, leading status syncs, navigating client feedback, and providing strategic production solutions. Agile Workflow & Daily Operations: Run daily scrums, triage incoming brief requests, and assign workloads to content managers, copywriters, and motion designers to keep daily social streams moving seamlessly. Financial Oversight & Costing: Lead end-to-end project costing, budgeting, financial forecasting, PO management, and cost reconciliation across high-volume retainer scopes and bespoke campaign spikes. Native Quality Control (QC): Perform meticulous quality control on all German-language social assets (static, video, motion graphics) to guarantee absolute linguistic accuracy, brand alignment, and cultural tone before client delivery. Retainer & Content Production: Oversee end-to-end execution of fast-turnaround social assets, localised multi-market campaigns, and platform-native video deliverables. Resourcing & Mentorship: Partner with Resource Management to cast internal teams and external freelancers effectively, while providing mentorship and workflow guidance to mid-level and junior team members. Qualifications Language Expertise: Native-level fluency in German (written and spoken) is required, along with full professional fluency in English. Social Retainer Background: Extensive experience in an agency environment managing high-volume, fast-turnaround social media retainers is a must. Project Management Synergy: While this is a Senior Integrated Producer role, candidates bringing a strong foundation or background in Project Management - experienced in running scrums, structuring workflows, and tracking deliverables - will be a natural fit. Financial Mastery: Proven proficiency in project costing, budget management, scope estimation, and financial risk mitigation. Client-Facing Mindset: Genuinely enjoys being client-facing and comfortable serving as the day-to-day operational contact for high-level brand partners. Rigorous QC Standards: An exceptional eye for detail, proofreading, and linguistic/visual quality assurance for social content. Experience delivering marketing or social campaigns within film, streaming, TV, or broader entertainment media. Exposure to live-action shoot production logistics and modern AI-driven production workflows. Note: We emphasise skills, expertise and behavioural attributes over years of experience and traditional degrees. If you want to join our collaborative team, we invite you to apply today with your resume in English. Additional Information Join Jellyfish and experience a workplace where we prioritise your growth, celebrate your contributions, and empower you to tailor your work environment to suit your needs. 💰 Reward: You'll be eligible to join our discretionary annual bonus scheme. 💫 Custom Work Environment: Work remotely for up to 60% of your days and shape your day between 8am. and 6:30pm with flexible working hours. Unfortunately, there has been an increase in fake recruiters impersonating Jellyfish and unlawfully using our brand name. If you are unsure if an email with a job offer you have received is genuinely from Jellyfish, or if you suspect any fraudulent activity, please report it to • €50K – €58K Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
