    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-producer-london-57675" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-11"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<p class=\"section-title\">As a Senior Producer, you are responsible for the effective management and delivery of projects, ensuring the best creative<br>solutions across a designated portfolio of clients are achieved in the most efficient, profitable and imaginable way for the Studio<br>while managing client expectations accordingly. You will be expected to lead production projects and delivery at Made Thought,<br>as the go-to in the team for Production led projects. You will play a vital role in building and nurturing relations with key industry<br>players, alongside lead creative, producing large productions on time and on budget. You must be creatively minded, and<br>understand how to carefully balance the flexibility required of a business with creativity at it’s core, alongside the rigour and strong<br>organisational skills which some of our clients can expect.</p> <p class=\"section-title\">&nbsp;</p> <p>RESPONSIBILITIES</p> <p class=\"section-title\">— Work collaboratively with the Creative team to actively ensure the best creative solutions are delivered against each client<br>brief. You will have the abilitiy to motivate people around you; both colleagues and clients, earning their trust and confidence.<br>— Run and manager a number of projects in the studio totalling circa £1-£1.5M per annum (inc third party productions costs).<br>You will be responsible for the allocation, planning and forecasting of all projects within your portfolio, ensuring they are set<br>up for the success from the outset.<br>— Be the key point of contact from Made Thought for all third parties related to the production process.<br>— Create a presence within the industry to ensure talent are keen to work with Made Thought and be actively seen as the<br>escalation point for production queries or issues within Made Thought.<br>— Be accountable for production project budgets and timings, ensuring the project is delivered on time to budget maintaining<br>an agreed project margin.</p> <p class=\"section-title\">— Utilising previous experience to think creatively and fluidly when providing solutions, escalating issues to Account Director or<br>Client Services when needed.<br>— Project dependent, support the Account Director (project lead) on larger / more complex projects to ensure all aspects of the<br>day-to-day are executed efficiently and effectively.<br>— Work with the Resource and Creative team to ensure the right team and timeline are in place. You will approach this<br>sensitively and intelligently to allow for profitability whilst protecting the creative process.<br>— Be accountable for your project commercials, with the ability to accurately scope, plan and deliver your projects on time,<br>working closely with the Finance Team to ensure projects are delivered on budget.<br>— Set and manage production budgets, to then provide weekly project status and cost reporting to the Finance and Client<br>Services Director.<br>— Forecasting production workflow for the upcoming quarter for your projects, highlighting any potential overruns before they<br>occur and proactively working with the team to reduce them.<br>— Conduct project wash-ups, sharing relevant findings with the wider team, and owning any improved ways of working<br>identified.<br>— Build strong and lasting relationships with our clients, maintaining regular contact to keep them updated on overall project<br>progress, highlighting any potential delays or scope for overspend. You will respond with speed and assurance to their<br>requests.<br>— Support new business on writing proposals and casting a team to suit your projects. You will also be accountable for creating<br>proposals from scratch (dependant on project size), seeking approval from Account Director where required.<br>Safeguard internal processes that protect Made Thought’s unique culture and creative output, while consistently looking for<br>and contributing towards improved processes and ways of working for the team.<br>— Research, suggest and inform the project team of which third parties should be used for the concept and will creatively<br>challenge in alignment with Made Thought’s creative ambition and budget / usage guidelines.<br>— Be accountable for ensuring usage rights are agreed and flagging when a touch point is approaching the end of a usage<br>period, negotiating extended usage accordingly.<br>— Use comprehensive knowledge of copyrights legislation on usage rights, and seek updated rules that govern usages to<br>ensure the company’s practices meets these standards.<br>— Oversee image checks, crediting, picture quality, repro for online and offline formats.<br>— Source new talent and production partners, build, update and maintain a MT production bank (including photographers,<br>directors, models, locations, studios, glam and set teams, and suppliers).<br>— Build strong relationships between Made Thought and shoot production industry (ie. Agents, production companies,<br>photographers, set designers and stylists).<br>— Manage and arrange commissioning of pre-existing assets from stock imagery to music, negotiating and agreeing usage as<br>necessary.<br>— Collaborate with internal creative team (AD / DD) to present relevant AD decks to clients throughout the production process<br>– ensuring creative expectations are in line / within client budget and overall scope of production.&nbsp;</p> <p class=\"section-title\">&nbsp;</p> <p class=\"section-title\">SKILLS &amp; EXPERIENCE</p> <p class=\"section-title\">— A rich portfolio of client relationships across multiple sectors, with proven experience of successfully nurturing and growing<br>client relationships.<br>— The ability to work seamlessly with others, leading by example and getting stuck in where needed.<br>— Bring demonstrable experience in developing and motivating teams, supporting people to reach their potential.<br>— Be able to balance the big picture with the detail, being able to think ahead and prioritse the workload for both yourself and<br>the team.<br>— Be a strong problem solver who does so with diplomacy and charm, and who considers the best outcomes for both client &amp;<br>agency.<br>— Have the ability to build trust within teams and inspire others.<br>— Exceptional standard of written and oral communication.</p> <div class=\"copy cms\">&nbsp;</div> <section class=\"panel\"></section><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><strong>About Made Thought</strong></p> <p>Made Thought is a like-minded collective of strategists, writers, thinkers, inventors, makers, dreamers, mavericks, rebels, connectors, instigators and igniters. We champion bold creativity and brave action underpinned by exceptional craft. From our studios in London and New York, we work with clients big and small who are open to change.&nbsp;</p> <p>We are proud to be part of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.madethought.com/news/introducing-the-new-standard\">The New Standard</a> (part of AKQA and WPP), an industry-leading collective of specialists from Made Thought, Universal Design Studio and Map Project Office.</p> <p class=\"x_x_x_MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p> <p class=\"x_x_x_MsoNormal\"><strong>About WPP&nbsp;</strong></p> <p class=\"x_x_x_MsoNormal\">WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel in a single company – powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open, to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><u><a href=\"http://wpp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" data-outlook-id=\"c63b46dc-df29-4f1e-af6a-35308b3cf773\">WPP.com</a></u>.</p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-madethought ;
