    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\">About Baringa&nbsp;</span></h3> <p>Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.</p> <p>The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence – all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.</p> <p>Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly – all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.</p> <p>Certified as a&nbsp;<em>Great Place to Work </em>around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the <em>Financial Times </em>in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by <em>Forbes </em>for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.</p></div><h3><span style=\"color: #00358e; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Baringa is looking for talented 2027 Summer Interns to join our Government &amp; Public Sector team!</span></h3> <h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">Our Internship</span></span></h3> <p>Our internship programmes will give you a first-hand view of life in an award-winning management consultancy firm. You will gain an understanding of the consulting business model as well as hands-on experience across the consulting project lifecycle, from understanding client challenges and analysing evidence through to developing recommendations and supporting delivery</p> <p>As an intern you will join a real team, working and learning from experienced consultants, with exposure to meaningful client work alongside a structured programme to learn more about Baringa and working as a consultant.</p> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">About the Government team at Baringa</span></h3> <p>Our Government team helps departments, agencies and public services solve complex problems and deliver better outcomes for citizens. Our work spans Central Government, Home Affairs, and Health and Public Infrastructure, from redesigning services and strengthening operations to using data, technology and AI to improve decisions and delivery.</p> <p>We work on Government’s most complex changes, partnering with departments across Whitehall and the wider public sector, using our skills in Strategy and Business Cases, Project Delivery, Operational Delivery, DDaT and Government Commercial.</p> <p>The UK public sector is navigating significant challenges and opportunities, including the delivery of major national priorities and missions. As our Public Sector team continues to grow, we are looking for curious and motivated interns who are excited to learn, contribute and develop with us. You do not need previous consulting or public sector experience – we are interested in how you approach problems, learn new things and apply your skills to real-world challenges.</p> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">What you will be doing</span></h3> <p>We will embed you in a project for your internship period, working alongside a team of experienced consultants to learn whilst delivering real client outcomes. You will not be expected to know how to do all of this from day one. You will be supported throughout and given opportunities to build your skills through meaningful project work.</p> <p>Depending on the project you join, you may have the opportunity to:</p> <ul> <li>Analyse quantitative and qualitative information to identify insights, trends and opportunities for improvement.</li> <li>Explore how data, digital technology, automation or AI could help improve public services.</li> <li>Develop recommendations and delivery plans, considering how people, technology and data work together.</li> <li>Support the development of client materials, including presentations, reports, workshop outputs and project updates.</li> <li>Contribute to meetings and workshop discussions, helping to capture key points, actions and decisions.</li> <li>Learn how consulting teams work together to solve problems, structure ambiguous challenges and communicate clearly with clients and colleagues.</li> </ul> <p>Examples of the type of projects you could be working on are:</p> <ul> <li>Support transformation projects that help government and public sector organisations improve services, strengthen operations and deliver better outcomes for citizens.</li> <li>Help review how services and processes work, from frontline delivery through to internal operations, identifying opportunities to make them simpler, more effective or more resilient.</li> <li>Contribute to digital, data and analytics work, including projects that use AI or data-led approaches to help clients make better decisions.</li> <li>Support the development of business cases and funding proposals, helping clients assess different options and make evidence-based decisions.</li> <li>Help design how services should operate, looking at how people, processes, technology and data come together to deliver better results within operating models and service blueprints.</li> <li>Support commercial and procurement activity, such as researching suppliers, comparing options and helping prepare materials for decision-making.</li> </ul> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">What are we looking for?</span></h3> <p>We welcome applications from students across a broad range of academic disciplines, including STEM and non-STEM subjects, and are particularly keen to hear from students who enjoy solving complex problems using evidence, data, technology and creative thinking. You do not need to have previous experience in consulting or the public sector - what matters most is your curiosity, willingness to learn and interest in helping public sector organisations solve complex challenges.</p> <p>We are looking for people who are excited by the opportunity to learn how consulting teams work, contribute to meaningful client projects and develop their skills in a supportive environment. You may be a good fit if you bring:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Structured problem solving</strong>, with the ability to break down unfamiliar questions and identify what matters.</li> <li><strong>Data analysis skills</strong>, and comfort working with data to surface insight and support evidence-based recommendations.&nbsp;</li> <li><strong>Digital and AI literacy</strong>, with genuine curiosity about AI and its practical application, and a foundational understanding of how to use these tools responsibly and ethically.</li> <li><strong>Interest in policy, government and public service</strong>, and how national priorities translate into delivery on the ground.</li> <li><strong>Commercial and financial curiosity</strong>, with an interest in how money, value and delivery decisions shape public services, and comfort working with numbers to support them.</li> <li><strong>Clear communication skills</strong>, including the ability to explain ideas simply and structure your thinking in writing and conversation.</li> <li><strong>A collaborative approach</strong>, with enthusiasm for working in teams and learning from others.</li> <li><strong>Willingness to learn and adapt</strong>, particularly in a fast-paced project environment where priorities can evolve.</li> <li><strong>Attention to detail and ownership</strong>, taking pride in the quality of your work and following through on tasks.</li> <li><strong>A proactive attitude</strong>, with the confidence to ask questions, contribute ideas and get involved.</li> </ul> <p>We do not expect you to have all the answers from day one. We are looking for potential, enthusiasm and a genuine interest in developing your consulting skills while contributing to work that matters.</p> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">What's in it for you?</span></h3> <p>An internship at Baringa is what you make it.</p> <p>This is an 8-week paid internship where you get real project experience alongside structured coaching and training with an opportunity to build your analytical, communication and problem-solving skills.</p> <p>You will leave the internship with practical consulting experience, a stronger understanding of public sector work, and a clearer view of whether consulting is the right career path for you. High performing interns may also be considered for a permanent role.</p> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">Requirements</span></h3> <p>Applicants should be in their penultimate year of their bachelor’s or master’s Degree studies. Applicants must have the permanent right to work in the UK now and in the future and be eligible for a UK Security Check (SC) clearance. All applicants will be asked for proof if invited to an assessment centre.</p> <p>Please note we’re unable to sponsor individuals for this opportunity.</p> <h3><span style=\"color: #00358e;\">Key dates</span></h3> <p>Application window closes: Monday 28<sup>th</sup> September 2026 at&nbsp;<u>12:00pm GMT</u><br>Assessment centres: w/c 30<sup>th</sup> November / 7<sup>th</sup> December<br>Internship start: Monday 5<sup>th</sup> July 2027<br>Internship end: Friday 27<sup>th</sup> August 2027</p> <p><em>This is a paid full-time internship.</em></p> <p>For further information, please read our <a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/graduate/pdfs-and-downloads/global-summer-internship-pack-2026.pdf\">Summer Internship 2027 pack</a></p> <h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">What a career at Baringa will give you</span> </span></h2> <h2><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\">Putting</span> </span><span data-contrast=\"none\"><span style=\"color: rgb(208, 0, 111);\">People</span> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">First.</span>&nbsp;</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:true,&quot;134233118&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:2,&quot;335559685&quot;:1320,&quot;335559738&quot;:200,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></h2> <h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\" data-contrast=\"none\">Diversity and Inclusion</span></h3> <p><span data-contrast=\"none\">We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe that creating an environment where everyone feels a sense of belonging is central to our culture and that diversity is paramount to driving creativity, innovation, and value for our clients and for our people.</span>&nbsp;</p> <h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\" data-contrast=\"none\">An award-winning workplace</span></h3> <p><span data-contrast=\"none\">You can be a part of our ‘Great Place to Work’ – with our commitment to women and well-being in the workplace for all. </span><a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/en/impact/awards/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">Click here</span></a><span data-contrast=\"none\"> to see some of our recent awards and how we’ve achieved this.</span>&nbsp;</p> <h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 53, 142);\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">Using business as a force for good.</span>&nbsp;</span></h3> <p><span data-contrast=\"none\">We maintain high standards of environmental performance and transparency, which can be seen through our commitment to Net Zero with our SBTI-verified Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions reduction targets and our support of the Better Business Act. We report our progress publicly and ensure that we are also externally assessed and scored through organisations like CDP and EcoVadis - helping us to continually identify where we can improve.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:200,&quot;335559739&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span data-contrast=\"none\">We have a long legacy of supporting the communities in which we work, and offer a variety of ways to contribute, by putting people first and creating impact that lasts. Our Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) agenda is about giving back to the communities in which we live and work by sharing our skills, talent and time. In essence, we aim to empower and encourage everyone in the firm to contribute to the things we care about, and support registered charities and organisations with a clear social or environmental purpose to increase the positive impact they can have.</span></p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(208, 0, 111); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\" data-teams=\"true\">Join us</span></h3> <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\" data-teams=\"true\">All applications received will be reviewed by a member of our Talent Acquisition team. We never rely solely on automated screening or AI tools to make hiring decisions. Your application will be considered for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, nationality, disability, age, faith or social background. We do not filter applications by university background and encourage those who have taken alternative educational and career paths to apply. We would like to actively encourage applications from those who identify with less represented and minority groups. We operate an inclusive recruitment process, ensuring reasonable adjustments where needed. Please contact a member of our Recruitment Team to discuss further.</span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <h3><span style=\"color: rgb(208, 0, 111); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\" data-teams=\"true\">Baringa Privacy Notices</span></h3> <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\"><strong>For UK &amp; EU</strong></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\">Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our <a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-004-ukrpn---uk-recruitment-privacy-notice-pdf.pdf\">UK Recruitment Privacy Notice / </a><a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-005-eurpn---eu-recruitment-privacy-notice-pdf.pdf\">EU Recruitment Privacy Notice</a>, to evaluate your application and meet our legal and reporting obligations. In line with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right to request access to, rectification, or erasure (subject to legal limitations) of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at <a ---------- <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\"><strong>For the USA</strong></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\">Your personal data may be retained by Baringa for up to two years, as outlined in our&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf\">Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp; APAC)</a>, to support the recruitment process and internal reporting requirements. Where applicable, and in accordance with relevant federal and state laws, you may have the right to request access to or correction of your personal information. For further details, please contact <a ---------- <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\"><strong>For Australia &amp; Singapore</strong></span></p> <p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\">Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our <a href=\"https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf\">Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp; APAC)</a>, to assess your application and meet applicable reporting and legal obligations. In line with the Australian Privacy Act and Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), you may have rights to access, correct, or request limited deletion of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at <a ---------- Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
