    schema:datePosted "2026-09-12"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About Peec AI Peec AI is the analytics platform for AI search. People increasingly discover products and make buying decisions through ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Google's AI Overviews instead of traditional search, and most brands have no idea where they show up in those answers. Peec gives marketing, SEO, and growth teams the data to see exactly that: how visible their brand is across AI platforms, how they compare to competitors, and where to win. We are defining this category, and the market is moving with us. Peec is a Series A company backed by 20VC and Singular, past $10M ARR, with a 80+ person team across our Berlin HQ and our new New York office. About the role We're looking for a Visiting Founders Associate to join our engineering team in Berlin. You'll be the operational backbone of the team, running the processes, projects, and internal work that keep everything moving, so our engineers can stay focused on building. The main piece of the role is our compliance work, which you'll coordinate and execute end to end. Around that sits everything else a fast-growing engineering team needs: internal IT, new tooling, team rituals, onboarding, and being the person the rest of the company comes to when they need something technical explained or unblocked. You'll get wide view of how a startup actually runs. What you’ll do Coordinate and execute our compliance work end to end. You will map what's needed, gather it, keep the timeline moving, close things out Support the wider team on compliance questions across engineering, GDPR, and data residency Help non-technical colleagues with technical things: production access, understanding our infrastructure, getting started with vibe-coding Improve developer experience. You will find what slows our engineers down and fix it Run the team operations: onboardings, engineering retros, team events, and invoice management What we’re looking for Currently pursuing or recently graduated from a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree Self-starter with a bias for action, eager to learn, and comfortable with ambiguity Some experience in a fast-paced environment (internship, working student role, or a startup) Exposure to project management, with several things moving at once and you keeping track of all of them A business, legal, or economics background paired with genuine technical comfort. You can find your way around a code base, docs, and developer tooling Available for 3-months Immediately available What we offer A high-impact internship working directly with the founders at one of Europe’s fastest-growing Series A startups Real ownership and visibility across the sales and revenue organization Regular team events and off-sites Paid Meal & Uber rides when working late The most beautiful office space and work environment in Berlin Compensation: €3K per month • €3K per month Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
